      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nSets `NCCL_RAS_ENABLE=0` for the MI355 mirror of \"Distributed DP + EP\". On the ROCm 10.0 (TheRock) stack (#58761) that job aborts at process exit.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Only the AMD (MI355) mirror's commands change; the H100 step is untouched.\n- On ROCm 7.2 this is a no-op, since RCCL 7.2.3 has no RAS thread.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Before: the job failed in 2 of 2 #58761 runs (ci #92942, #93360).\n- After: it passed in #58761's ci retry #93436 with this change.\n- It does not reproduce on MI300X (15 clean runs on ROCm 10, 8-rank and 4-rank, plus 1 on 7.2), so CI is the only signal. One pass is not proof for an exit-time race; more runs will tell.\n\n## Details\n\nAll 8 ranks print correct generations. Then, after Python exits, 1 to 3 ranks hit `terminate called without an active exception` (SIGABRT, `<no Python frame>`): a `std::thread` destroyed while still joinable.\n- RCCL is never shut down at exit. vLLM's exit cleanup runs `ncclCommAbort` on a background thread and waits only 5 s for it, and a thread dump at exit showed that thread still in `ncclCommAbort`.\n- RCCL 2.30.4 (ROCm 10 SDK) has a global RAS `std::thread` that RCCL 7.2.3 lacks.\n- Its `rasTerminate()` only joins the thread if sending the stop message succeeds. That failure plausibly depends on pod networking, which would explain MI355-only.\n\nThe RAS diagnosis is inferred from disassembly; nobody has captured the native stack on MI355 yet. An RCCL issue will follow.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
